DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: York County Registry of Deeds
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + Spring/summer online debut planned for historical York County records
 \n  + ALFRED\, Maine – In May 1835\, Ivory R. Hatch\, who lived in the t
 own of Wells\, was unhappy with the result of an interaction with the town
  concerning a portion of his land. Wells selectmen had undertaken to lay o
 ut a road – an important decision at a time when there weren’t many ro
 ads. The new road\, to be 3 rods\, or 49.5 feet wide\, was to be built on 
 several portions of privately held land – including 72 rods\, or 1\,188 
 feet – of Hatch’s property. “Aggrieved\,” in the amount of\n  + Ta
 mmy L Wells\n  + 1 day ago\n  + 4 min read\nRemoved:\n  - Seeing history\,
  up close\n  - While people drive by the 1806 York County Court House in A
 lfred every day\, many may have never been inside\, and fewer still may kn
 ow how much history lives in this county-owned building.\n  - Tammy L Well
 s\n  - Oct 2\, 2025\n  - 6 min read\nhttps://www.yorkcountymaine.gov/regis
 try-of-deeds
URL:https://www.yorkcountymaine.gov/registry-of-deeds
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
